# Typhoid Rats (1/1, Deathtouch) attacks; Durkwood Boars (4/4, no keywords)
# blocks. No fixture exercises Deathtouch at all today. The Rats' single
# point of damage is lethal to the Boars regardless of its 4 toughness --
# CR 702.2b, destroyDamagedCreatures reading the deathtouch flag
# dealPermanentDamage set on the mark, not the raw amount against toughness
# (the removed port log's "Lethal and deathtouch damage" section). The Boars' 4
# damage back is ordinary-lethal to the Rats' own 1 toughness regardless --
# both die to the same state-based-action check.
startturn human
advance 5
queue attackers 1
declareattackers
advance
queue blocks 2=1
declareblockers
advance
advance
combatdamage
# One more advance for the state-based-action check that moves both
# lethally damaged creatures to the graveyard.
advance
